Design+verification pass for Branch B (operator-directed). Branch B's mechanism = condition the
representation/proposal on interaction-history to recover the hidden order-state. ALREADY BUILT + NULLED:
- exp4893 action_prefix_latent_adapter (.451 A1b): latent_substrate=action_prefix_future_state (the
  action-prefix = interaction history), 9 held-out games -> complete_action_prefix_latent_no_value_lift_
  representation_invariant_hard, delta median 0.0, CI95 [-0.135, 0.025]. Interaction-history conditioning
  recovers NO signal. exp4914's order-state is 'interaction-dependent classification ground truth' --
  definable only relative to the UNKNOWN solution, not a learnable function of observable experience.

So BOTH branches are already executed + refuted by the .451-.454 chain (Branch A exp4883 METHOD_IS_CEILING
+ Branch B exp4893 REPRESENTATION_INVARIANT_HARD; supported by exp4892/4903/4904/4914). The directed-
generation/representation program was already run systematically. No un-run cheapest-decisive probe remains
in the induce/plan/condition-on-observable family.

HONEST CONCLUSION (doc STATUS banner + §5): the generation wall is INFORMATION-THEORETIC (gradient-free
first-contact needle-search; the order-state isn't in the frame, in action-history, or in 4 representation
classes), not lever-shaped. Generic first-win 1/25 = the games stumble-able blindly. Thin residuals
(history-keyed model-free dedup; AMAGO unbuilt) are low-EV. Realistic paradigm-change options
(strong-inducer-as-live-agent = offline-illegal; bigger local model = engineering, likely moot per
hidden-state) are not deadline-week levers. Recommendation: treat live multi-level ARC generation as a
closed honest-negative for the current paradigm; deliverable stays 0.08 + FoVer paper.

Lesson reinforced (and banked in the doc): run the exclusion/rerun check BEFORE designing a build. It
caught BOTH branches as re-runs this session.

